---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="How It Works — CircuitBot" description="Learn how CircuitBot turns your game idea into a playable Godot 4 project with AI-generated art, code, and a compiled build.">

  <section class="section hiw-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="badge badge-blue">How It Works</span>
        <h1>From Idea to <span class="gradient-text">Playable Game</span></h1>
        <p class="hiw-subtitle">Three steps. One prompt. A real game you can play and learn from.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- Steps -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hiw-steps">

        <div class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-number">1</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-content">
            <h2>Describe Your Game</h2>
            <p>
              Write a few sentences about the game you want to build. Describe the genre, mechanics,
              art style, enemies, levels — whatever you imagine. The more detail you give, the better
              the result.
            </p>
            <div class="hiw-example">
              <div class="hiw-example-label">Example prompt</div>
              <p>"A retro pixel-art roguelike dungeon crawler with procedural levels, three enemy types, and a boss fight at the end of each floor."</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-number">2</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-content">
            <h2>We Build It</h2>
            <p>
              CircuitBot's AI plans the game architecture, generates all the art assets (sprites,
              tilesets, backgrounds), writes the complete <span style="color: var(--accent-blue);">GDScript</span> code, assembles everything in
              <span style="color: var(--accent-blue);">Godot 4</span>, and compiles a playable build. This takes about 15-30 minutes.
            </p>
            <ul class="hiw-detail-list">
              <li>Custom AI-generated 2D art assets</li>
              <li>Full game logic — movement, combat, UI, menus</li>
              <li>Properly structured Godot project with scenes and scripts</li>
              <li>Compiled Windows executable</li>
              <li>Web-playable build you can share instantly</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-number">3</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-content">
            <h2>Play, Learn, and Build On It</h2>
            <p>
              Download the full <span style="color: var(--accent-blue);">Godot 4</span> project. Play your game, read the code, tweak things,
              break things, and learn by doing. This is a real starting point — not a demo.
              You own everything and can take it in any direction.
            </p>
            <ul class="hiw-detail-list">
              <li>Open in the Godot editor and modify anything</li>
              <li>Study the GDScript code to learn game dev patterns</li>
              <li>Request edits through CircuitBot to iterate further</li>
              <li>Full commercial ownership — sell it, share it, open-source it</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- What's Inside -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>What Is Inside <span class="gradient-text">Your Game</span></h2>
        <p>Every generated game comes with real, editable source code you can learn from.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card feature-card">
          <h3><span class="feature-icon">&#127912;</span> Custom Art</h3>
          <p>AI-generated sprites, textures, and backgrounds that match your game's visual style.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card feature-card">
          <h3><span class="feature-icon">&#128187;</span> Real Code</h3>
          <p>Complete GDScript you can read and learn from — player movement, enemies, scoring, and more.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card feature-card">
          <h3><span class="feature-icon">&#127760;</span> UI &amp; Menus</h3>
          <p>Title screens, HUD, health bars, and score displays — all properly structured in Godot scenes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card feature-card">
          <h3><span class="feature-icon">&#128736;</span> Scene Architecture</h3>
          <p>Properly organized Godot project with correct node hierarchies you can study and extend.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card feature-card">
          <h3><span class="feature-icon">&#127916;</span> Input Handling</h3>
          <p>Keyboard and controller mappings pre-configured for your game's mechanics.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card feature-card">
          <h3><span class="feature-icon">&#128640;</span> Playable Build</h3>
          <p>A compiled Windows .exe ready to share with friends — no engine installation needed to play.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bottom CTA -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-bottom:80px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Ready to <span class="gradient-text">Build</span>?</h2>
        <p>Your first game is free. Describe your idea and have a playable build in minutes.</p>
        <a href="/create" class="btn btn-yellow btn-lg" style="margin-top:24px;">Create Your Free Game</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .hiw-hero {
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .hiw-subtitle {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .hiw-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 48px;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hiw-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .hiw-step-number {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(69, 130, 199, 0.1);
    border: 2px solid var(--accent-blue);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .hiw-step-content h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .hiw-step-content p {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .hiw-example {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 16px 20px;
  }

  .hiw-example-label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .hiw-example p {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .hiw-detail-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .hiw-detail-list li {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding: 4px 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .hiw-detail-list li::before {
    content: "\2713 ";
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-right: 8px;
  }

  .feature-card {
    padding: 28px 24px;
  }

  .feature-icon {
    font-size: 22px;
    vertical-align: middle;
    margin-right: 4px;
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .hiw-step {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .hiw-step-number {
      width: 36px;
      height: 36px;
      font-size: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
